822:     /**
823:      * Implementations of this method should register/unregister the fig for all
824:      * (model)events. For FigEdgeModelElement only the fig itself is registered
825:      * as listening to events fired by the owner itself. But for, for example,
826:      * FigAssociation the fig must also register for events fired by the
827:      * stereotypes of the owner. <p>
828:      * 
829:      * This function is used in UMLDiagram, which removes all listeners 
830:      * to all Figs when a diagram is not displayed, and restore them
831:      * when it becomes visible again. <p>
832:      * 
833:      * In this case, it is not imperative that indeed ALL listeners are 
834:      * updated, as long as the ones removed get added again and vice versa. <p>
835:      * 
836:      * Additionally, this function may be used by the modelChanged() function.
837:      * <p>
838:      * 
839:      * In this case, it IS imperative that all listeners get removed / added.
840:      * 
841:      * @param newOwner the new owner for the listeners
842:      */
843:     protected void updateListeners(Object oldOwner, Object newOwner) {
844:         if (oldOwner == newOwner) {
845:             LOG.warn("Listeners being added and removed from the same owner");
846:         }
847:         if (oldOwner != null) {
848:             removeElementListener(oldOwner);
849:         }
850:         if (newOwner != null) {
851:             addElementListener(newOwner);
852:         }
853:     }
