Has the original ask been met?  
No. While the variable list in initMenuCreateModelElements was renamed to menuItems, other “action”–related names remain misleading in a UI context and have not been renamed to more descriptive “menu” terms.  

What needs to be changed:  
- Line 78:  
  Rename  
    private JMenu createDiagrams   
  to  
    private JMenu createDiagramMenu;  

- Line 276 (and its call on line 126):  
  Rename method  
    private void initMenuCreateDiagrams()  
  to  
    private void initCreateDiagramMenu()  
  and update its invocation at line 126 accordingly:  
    initCreateDiagramMenu();  

- Line 296 (and its call on line 131):  
  Rename method  
    private void initMenuCreateModelElements()  
  to  
    private void initCreateModelElementsMenu()  
  and update its invocation at line 131 accordingly:  
    initCreateModelElementsMenu();  

- Line 327:  
  Rename local variable  
    JMenu menu = new JMenu("Create Model Element");  
  to something like  
    JMenu modelElementsMenu = new JMenu("Create Model Element");  
