818:     /**
819:      * Implementations of this method should register/unregister the fig for all
820:      * (model)events. For FigEdgeModelElement only the fig itself is registered
821:      * as listening to events fired by the owner itself. But for, for example,
822:      * FigAssociation the fig must also register for events fired by the
823:      * stereotypes of the owner. <p>
824:      * 
825:      * This function is used in UMLDiagram, which removes all listeners 
826:      * to all Figs when a diagram is not displayed, and restore them
827:      * when it becomes visible again. <p>
828:      * 
829:      * In this case, it is not imperative that indeed ALL listeners are 
830:      * updated, as long as the ones removed get added again and vice versa. <p>
831:      * 
832:      * Additionally, this function may be used by the modelChanged() function.
833:      * <p>
834:      * 
835:      * In this case, it IS imperative that all listeners get removed / added.
836:      * 
837:      * @param newOwner the new owner for the listeners
838:      */
839:     protected void updateListeners(Object newOwner) {
840:         Object oldOwner = getOwner();
841:         if (oldOwner != null) {
842:             removeElementListener(oldOwner);
843:         }
844:         if (newOwner != null) {
845:             addElementListener(newOwner);
846:         }
847:     }
