91:  * Facade object for the Model component in ArgoUML.<p>
92:  *
93:  * The purpose of this Facade object is to allow for decoupling other modules
94:  * from the insides of the model. For this purpose all of the methods in this
95:  * class give away and accept handles (of type java.lang.Object) to the
96:  * objects within the model.<p>
97:  *
98:  * This is just getters and recognizers. This is because the Model
99:  * component has an extremely complicated internal data structure
100:  * with lots of internal dependencies. To manipulate these there is
101:  * a whole set of factories and helpers within the Model that is to
102:  * be used but to use them you need knowledge of the internals of
103:  * the Model, specifically the NS-UML objects.<p>
104:  *
105:  * All methods in this facade are static.<p>
106:  *
107:  * Signature for all recognizers in this Facade:
108:  * public static boolean isA<TYPE>(Object handle)
109:  * public static boolean is<PROPERTY>(Object handle)
110:  * <p>
111:  *
112:  * Signature for all getters in this Facade:
113:  * public static Object get<TYPE>(Object handle) - 1..1
114:  * public static Iterator get<TYPES>(Object handle) - 0..*
115:  * public static String getName(Object handle) - Name
116:  * <p>
117:  *
118:  * @stereotype utility
119:  * @author Linus Tolke
120:  */
